---
/**
 * Lyžování v okolí   nearby ski areas.
 *
 * Rewrites docs/01-content.md §7.3: "REWRITE   same treatment. Distances and
 * drive times." Most distances are not available yet.
 *
 * DATA: src/data/okoli.ts LYZOVANI. Only the first entry (Dolní Morava) has a
 * verified distance   it is the one in the distance table (§5.2). The remaining
 * six entries have vzdalenost: null and cas: null and will stay that way until
 * the client supplies the figures.
 *
 * TODO(client)   docs/01-content.md §9 item 21: distances for the remaining ski
 * areas. Once they arrive, add vzdalenost and cas to each entry in LYZOVANI in
 * src/data/okoli.ts, and this section becomes seven rows of the catalogue shape
 * OkoliVylety.astro uses rather than one statement and a run of names.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * WHY ONE BIG LINE AND A RUN OF NAMES
 *
 * This section has been a bordered panel and then a two-column split, and the
 * honest description of its content defeats both: it is ONE ski area anybody can
 * plan around, and six place names nobody has measured. A panel gives the six
 * names a container that implies they are data. A split gives them a column,
 * which implies they are half the section.
 *
 * They are a footnote. So Dolní Morava is set as a single statement across the
 * full measure   the name in the display face, the two figures under it at the
 * size of a heading, because on a page whose entire argument is distances those
 * two numbers ARE the content   and the six others are a plain run separated by
 * middots, the way a guidebook sets a list of names it has nothing further to say
 * about. The run is deliberately not a list with rules and marks: rules and marks
 * would be columns, and columns are a promise of data in each one.
 *
 * It is also the one section on this page with no repeating unit at all. Between
 * a catalogue of six rows above and a pair of figures plus ten names below, the
 * page needs one beat that is a single object.
 *
 * ---- THE TILE, AT THREE SCALES ----
 * OkoliVylety.astro pairs every row with a photo-or-icon tile (OkoliMedia.astro).
 * The same idea repeats here at the scale this section's content earns it: a
 * large tile beside the one statement   a real photograph, the only one on the
 * page usable for a ski area   and a small inline snowflake before each of the
 * six unmeasured names, never a tile of their own. A tile per unmeasured name
 * would be six placeholders in a row, which is the bordered-panel mistake again
 * in icon form; one mark per name is the same footnote treatment the middots
 * already give them, just with something to look at as well as read.
 *
 * WHY --jinovatka FOR THIS SECTION
 * docs/02-design-system.md §1 reserves --jinovatka as a WINTER ACCENT ONLY  
 * ski content, snow content, and the cold months of the calendar. The design
 * system is explicit that this is one of the very few places it may appear.
 * A full section background reads as a clear, immediate visual signal: "this
 * is the ski section." No other section on this page may use this colour.
 *
 * Contrast on --jinovatka:
 *   --les text:        12.17:1  (the statement, the run of names)
 *   --kura text:        9.39:1  (descriptions, the note)
 *   --mosaz-tmava text: 4.81:1  (headings, figures)   passes the 4.5:1 floor ✓
 *
 * Band: --jinovatka. Follows --omitka (vylety) and precedes --kamen (koupani).
 */
import { LYZOVANI } from '../../../data/okoli';
import IconLucide from '../../IconLucide.astro';
import OkoliMedia from './OkoliMedia.astro';

/* U+00A0   non-breaking space. */
const NBSP = ' ';

/* The first entry is the only one with a verified distance. */
const [dolniMorava, ...ostatni] = LYZOVANI;
---

<section class="lyzovani section" aria-labelledby="lyzovani-nadpis">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="lyzovani-header" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="lyzovani-nadpis">Lyžování v okolí</h2>
    </header>

    {/* ---- The one area anybody can plan around ---- */}
    <div class="lyzovani-hlavni" data-reveal>
      <OkoliMedia icon="cable-car" foto={dolniMorava.foto} class="lyzovani-media" />

      <div class="lyzovani-hlavni-text">
        <p class="lyzovani-stitek">
          <IconLucide name="cable-car" size={16} />
          <span>Nejbližší středisko</span>
        </p>

        <h3 class="lyzovani-nazev">{dolniMorava.nazev}</h3>

        {/*
          The figures, set at heading size and side by side under a brass rule.
          Not `aria-hidden`: `9 km vzdušnou čarou` and `12 min autem` are the only
          place in this section those two facts are stated, so hiding them would
          delete them from the accessibility tree. It is a real definition list.
        */}
        {(dolniMorava.vzdalenost || dolniMorava.cas) && (
          <dl class="lyzovani-fakta">
            {dolniMorava.vzdalenost && (
              <div>
                <dt>{dolniMorava.vzdalenost}</dt>
                <dd>vzdušnou čarou</dd>
              </div>
            )}
            {dolniMorava.cas && (
              <div>
                <dt>{dolniMorava.cas}</dt>
                <dd>autem z chalupy</dd>
              </div>
            )}
          </dl>
        )}

        <p class="lyzovani-popis">
          Deset kilometrů sjezdovek s umělým zasněžováním, Stezka{NBSP}v oblacích, Sky
          Bridge{NBSP}721, bobová dráha a dětské zábavní areály.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* ---- The rest: names, and honestly nothing else ---- */}
    {ostatni.length > 0 && (
      <div class="lyzovani-ostatni" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="lyzovani-ostatni-nadpis">Další střediska v okolí</h3>
        <p class="lyzovani-ostatni-pozn">
          Vzdálenosti k těmto střediskům zatím nejsou ověřeny, a proto zde nejsou uvedeny.
        </p>
        {/*
          A run, not a list with rules and marks. See the header comment: giving
          six unmeasured place names a column each promises a figure in every one
            a tile each would be the same mistake in icon form. One small
          snowflake per name is the supporting mark this run gets instead.

          It is still a <ul>   it is a list, and a screen reader should say so and
          count it. The snowflake is `aria-hidden`; the middots are `::before`
          content on `li + li`, so neither is announced, and the accessibility
          tree hears six plain names.
        */}
        <ul class="lyzovani-run" role="list">
          {ostatni.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <IconLucide name="snowflake" size={13} class="lyzovani-run-ikona" />
              <span>{s.nazev}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    )}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lyzovani {
    /*
     * docs/02-design-system.md §1: --jinovatka is a winter accent only   ski
     * content, snow, cold months. This is one of the very few places it may
     * legitimately appear as a section background.
     */
    background-color: var(--color-jinovatka);
  }

  h2,
  h3 {
    /* --mosaz-tmava on --jinovatka = 4.81:1   the tightest passing case here. */
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
  }

  /* ---- The statement -----------------------------------------------------
   *
   * A flex pair from the smallest viewport up   tile then text   same motif as
   * `.vylety-radek`'s tile-plus-body, at a scale that matches this section's one
   * object. `align-items: flex-start` keeps the tile pinned to the top when the
   * text block grows taller than it on a phone.
   */
  .lyzovani-hlavni {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-mosaz);
  }

  .lyzovani-media {
    width: 5.5rem;
  }

  @media (width >= 48rem) {
    .lyzovani-media {
      width: 8rem;
    }
  }

  @media (width >= 64rem) {
    .lyzovani-media {
      width: 10rem;
    }
  }

  .lyzovani-hlavni-text {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /*
   * A label rather than a heading: it says which of the seven areas this is,
   * which the name alone does not. Caption size, brass, uppercase tracking   the
   * one place on the page it appears, so it reads as a tag on a single object
   * rather than as a section eyebrow the site stamps on everything.
   */
  .lyzovani-stitek {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    /* --mosaz-tmava on --jinovatka = 4.81:1 */
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
  }

  .lyzovani-nazev {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: var(--text-title-m);
    line-height: 1.15;
    max-width: 20ch;
    /* --les on --jinovatka = 12.17:1 */
    color: var(--color-les);
  }

  @media (width >= 64rem) {
    .lyzovani-nazev {
      /* The section's one object, at the size of a page heading. There is no h2
         competing with it   `Lyžování v okolí` sits above the rule at title-l and
         this is the thing under it. */
      font-size: var(--text-title-l);
    }
  }

  .lyzovani-fakta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem 3.5rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
  }

  .lyzovani-fakta dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--text-title-m);
    line-height: 1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
  }

  .lyzovani-fakta dd {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    line-height: 1.4;
    /* --kura on --jinovatka = 9.39:1 */
    color: var(--color-kura);
  }

  .lyzovani-popis {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    max-width: 46ch;
    color: var(--color-kura);
  }

  /* ---- The footnote ------------------------------------------------------ */

  .lyzovani-ostatni {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.75rem;
    /* A hairline, not the 2px brass rule above: this is subordinate to the
       statement, and the weight of the rule is what says so. */
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(22 36 28 / 0.14);
  }

  .lyzovani-ostatni-nadpis {
    font-size: var(--text-title-s);
  }

  .lyzovani-ostatni-pozn {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    max-width: 56ch;
    /* --kura on --jinovatka = 9.39:1 */
    color: var(--color-kura);
  }

  .lyzovani-run {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    /* --les on --jinovatka = 12.17:1 */
    color: var(--color-les);
  }

  /*
   * Each `<li>` is its own inline-flex row of icon + name, so the snowflake sits
   * on the text baseline instead of stacking above it   `svg { display: block }`
   * in global.css would otherwise drop it onto its own line.
   */
  .lyzovani-run li {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4em;
  }

  .lyzovani-run-ikona {
    flex: none;
    /* --mosaz-tmava on --jinovatka = 4.81:1 */
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
  }

  /*
   * ⚠ The middot goes BEFORE each name after the first, never after each name
   * before the last. It is inside the <li>, so it wraps with the name it belongs
   * to: put it in `::after` and a wrapped line ends on a dangling brass dot with
   * nothing following it, which reads as a typo. Leading it means a wrapped line
   * begins with the mark, which reads as a continued list.
   */
  .lyzovani-run li + li::before {
    content: '·';
    margin-inline: 0 0.75em;
    color: var(--color-mosaz);
  }

  .lyzovani-run li + li {
    /* The gap the ::before does not provide on the left of the mark itself. */
    margin-left: 0.75em;
  }
</style>
